# Purpose
Keep the app compatible with Expo tooling and EAS. Handle permissions/config correctly and avoid accidental native breakage.

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO treat app.json / app.config.* as the authoritative config surface. (Verify which one the repo uses before editing.)
DO handle permissions as build-time configuration + runtime UX:
  - Configure Android permissions via android.permissions / android.blockedPermissions only when needed.
  - Request permissions just-in-time and handle denial with a user-friendly fallback.
DO prefer Expo SDK APIs over adding native dependencies.
DO if adding any dependency that touches native code:
  - Provide rationale
  - Document required config plugin changes (if any)
  - Explicitly state EAS build implications (dev build / production build)

### DON'T
MUST NOT request broad permissions at startup.
MUST NOT add native modules when an Expo module exists for the same capability.
MUST NOT change config keys without citing the exact file/section changed.

## Completion Checklist
[ ] Config edited in the correct config file (after confirming which one is used).
[ ] Permissions are least-privilege and requested only when needed.
[ ] Native-dep additions include rationale + EAS implications.
[ ] npx expo doctor is included in verification steps.

## Common Pitfalls
Works in Expo Go but fails in dev/production builds due to missing native config.
Adding permissions that trigger store review friction without necessity.
Adding a native dependency without acknowledging that it requires EAS builds.
